<title>RUSSIA: Russia to offer 10.50 trln rbls T-bills Sept 4.</title>
<headline>Russia to offer 10.50 trln rbls T-bills Sept 4.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian finance ministry will offer 3.50 trillion roubles of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills and 7.00 trillion roubles of six-month bills on September 4, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Three-month bills:</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     3.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				121 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			 Sept 4, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity			   Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>Non-residents are allowed to buy up to 10 percent of the nominal amount of the issue.</p>
<p>Six-month bills:</p>
<p>    Issue volume		     7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor				217 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			 Sept 4, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity			   April 9, 1997</p>
<p>Non-residents are allowed to buy up to 35 percent of the nominal amount of the issue.</p>
<p>The bills actually run for four and seven months respectively, but officially classified as three and six-month paper by the central bank.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
